# U2-D2716.bin (Ampex D-175 detached keyboard, INS8039 firmware) — symbol overlay.
#
# Curated by hand. Regenerate U2.asm with:
#   make U2.asm
#
# Format:
#   HHHH NAME           ; optional comment
#   NAME EQU $HHHH      ; for non-code addresses (RAM aliases, etc.)
#   +entry HHHH         ; force the decoder to start tracing at HHHH
#                       ; (use when a code block is reached only via
#                       ; JMPP @A and would otherwise be left as data)
#
# All claims here are working hypotheses pending Phase 1 hardware tracing
# (see ../REVERSE_ENGINEERING_PLAN.md). Update freely as analysis proceeds.

# ---- Reset / interrupt vectors ---------------------------------------------
0000 RESET                 ; cold-start: DIS I ; JMP MAIN_INIT
0003 IRQ_EXT               ; external (INT) — currently DIS I ; RETR (unused?)
0007 IRQ_TIMER             ; timer/counter ISR — heart of the scan/tick loop

# ---- Main init -------------------------------------------------------------
0100 MAIN_INIT             ; entered from RESET via JMP at $0001

# ---- External data-bus scan loop ------------------------------------------
# Iterates R7 from $30..$3C, using R7 both as the internal-RAM source index
# (latest scan state) and as the external bus low-address byte. P2's upper
# nibble supplies the upper bus address bits (TBD by Phase 1 schematic). Each
# iteration writes a byte to and reads a byte from a single external location
# — almost certainly the GI U1 keyboard-scanner data port. Result byte goes
# into R5, then handler at $01D0 processes it.
00E4 SCAN_GI_PORT          ; CALL site for the scan loop (called from main)
00EB SCAN_GI_PORT_LOOP
01D0 PROC_SCAN_BYTE        ; consumes one byte returned from the GI scanner
